// TEST: ML Galilean Suggest Velocity Difference
import ml as ml
// ============================================================================
// THE FULL-SET CANDIDATE — the one non-singleton slice of the hypothesis space
// v1 searches, and the reason it exists.
//
// `slip_energy` is the velocity-DIFFERENCE shape, and every singleton
// hypothesis necessarily fails on it:
//
//   {uc}:  uc - ub  is  BVar - BInv = BVar, and squaring a boost-variant value
//          scales its U0-coefficient — BL4009, no proposal.
//   {ub}:  uc - ub  is  BInv - BVar, which carries U0-coefficient -1 — the
//          judgment refuses it outright (v2's rational coefficients will not).
//
// The theorem is nonetheless true, and it is true JOINTLY: boost BOTH cells by
// the same U0 and the difference is unchanged. So when no singleton passes and
// at least two parameters occur free, the channel tries the FULL occurring set
// once — `BVar - BVar -> BInv`, the central rule of this lattice — and proposes
// `galilean(uc, ub)`. Intermediate subsets are not searched: the combinatorics
// buy nothing on the bodies this exists for, and every skipped subset is
// silence, which is always sound.
//
// Note the ORDER in the message: parameters are listed in declaration order,
// not discovery order, so the suggestion reads as the clause the user types.
//
// The twin is below, and the numerical shadow is inline: the same call with
// both cells boosted by U0 = 10 returns the identical value.
//
// The suggestion channel IS this test, so the warning it emits is an assertion.
// WARN: BL4014
// ============================================================================

// SUGGEST: function 'slip_energy' judges boost-invariant with velocity parameter(s) uc, ub: add 'where ml.galilean(uc, ub)'
function slip_energy(uc: Float, ub: Float) -> Float = {
    let d = uc - ub
    d * d
}

// The pinned twin: the proposal, written out, and checked.
function slip_energy_pinned(uc: Float, ub: Float) where ml.galilean(uc, ub) -> Float = {
    let d = uc - ub
    d * d
}

let e = slip_energy(3.0, 1.0)
// EXPECT: e = 4.0
let e_boosted = slip_energy(13.0, 11.0)
// EXPECT: e_boosted = 4.0
let p = slip_energy_pinned(3.0, 1.0)
// EXPECT: p = 4.0
let p_boosted = slip_energy_pinned(13.0, 11.0)
// EXPECT: p_boosted = 4.0
